      "side": 1,
      "message": "Upon experimentation, I found that __FILE__ expands to whatever path, relative or absolute, was passed to the compiler.  LLVM (or it could be CMake in general) uses absolute paths during build and we need `-fmacro-prefix-map` or `-ffile-prefix-map`.  `-fdebug-compilation-dir .` doesn\u0027t help in this aspect.\n\nPlatform build only uses relative paths (including for `-I`) so I think `-fmacro-prefix-map` is unnecessary.  `-fdebug-compilation-dir` does the right job for the RBE use case, so +1 to doing that if necessary.",
